Nico once (5th March 1991) remarked that it struck him as odd that =
tagging
of \bibitems is done outside LaTeX.

I was invited to submit some comments to the Text Encoding Initiative =
about
how they might treat references and citations (in spite of my lack of
knowledge of TEI and SGML!).  My attempt to produce something for them
involved some consideration that is analogous to "if \bibitems were =
tagged
internally, what structures might have to be tagged internally?".  This
somewhat tenuous link is why my next mail will be a copy of the notes I =
did
for TEI.  [I think that the file is about 45K, so should get through
mailers OK.]

                                                                      =
David


